from (values
('127.94.d.8.D',4,'If actual spending is above the budget, the manager should:','["Ignore it", "Hide it", "Stop tracking", "Investigate and adjust the plan"]'::jsonb,3,'Control actions fix variances.','original'),
('127.94.d.8.E',3,'Closing a project includes:','["Final inspections, punch list, and handoff", "Skipping documentation", "Starting over", "Ignoring defects"]'::jsonb,0,'Closeout completes the job.','original'),
('127.94.d.8.E',4,'A ''lessons learned'' review at closeout helps teams to:','["Skip reflection", "Improve future projects", "Repeat mistakes", "Blame people"]'::jsonb,1,'Learning from experience improves performance.','original'),
('127.94.d.9.A',3,'Experienced planners include extra time in the schedule for:','["Nothing", "Holidays only", "Weather and material delays", "Lunch only"]'::jsonb,2,'Buffers absorb disruptions.','original'),
('127.94.d.9.A',4,'Allowing a contingency in the timeline helps to:','["Ignore risk", "Delay the start", "Add costs only", "Stay on track when problems occur"]'::jsonb,3,'Contingency protects schedules.','original'),
('127.94.d.9.B',3,'An event that could delay a framing crew is:','["Heavy rain", "A sunny day", "A clear schedule", "A full inspection pass"]'::jsonb,0,'Weather often disrupts outdoor work.','original'),
('127.94.d.9.B',4,'A late lumber delivery can disrupt a job because it:','["Speeds the work", "Stops framing from starting", "Reduces inspections", "Adds crews"]'::jsonb,1,'Delivery delays hold up tasks.','original'),
('127.94.d.9.C',3,'If a supplier is out of stock, the project manager should:','["Stop the job", "Wait indefinitely", "Find an alternative source or product", "Hide the problem"]'::jsonb,2,'Solve unexpected problems.','original'),
('127.94.d.9.C',4,'When an unexpected change order arrives, the manager should:','["Ignore it", "Do it silently", "Delay the answer", "Assess its impact and communicate it"]'::jsonb,3,'Respond with analysis.','original'),
('127.94.d.9.D',3,'Adjusting a schedule after a delay means:','["Re-sequencing tasks and moving dates", "Ignoring the delay", "Quitting", "Deleting the plan"]'::jsonb,0,'Adjustments keep the project viable.','original'),
('127.94.d.9.D',4,'If drywall is delayed a week, a manager might:','["Send everyone home", "Shift other tasks forward to keep crews busy", "Cancel the project", "Skip inspections"]'::jsonb,1,'Flexible sequencing saves time.','original'),
('127.94.d.9.E',3,'Modifying an existing plan after an unexpected change requires:','["Destroying the plan", "Nothing", "Updating dates, resources, and communication", "Ignoring it"]'::jsonb,2,'Revised plans reflect new conditions.','original'),
('127.94.d.9.E',4,'After a design change, all trades should receive:','["No notice", "Rumors", "The old plan only", "The revised plan or schedule"]'::jsonb,3,'Everyone needs current information.','original'),
('127.94.d.9.F',3,'A critical situation on a jobsite should be:','["Identified quickly and assessed", "Hidden", "Delayed", "Ignored"]'::jsonb,0,'Prompt response prevents harm.','original'),
('127.94.d.9.F',4,'When a trench wall starts to crumble, the right action is to:','["Keep working", "Evacuate and secure the area", "Take photos", "Add more digging"]'::jsonb,1,'Safety first in emergencies.','original'),
('127.94.d.9.G',3,'A project update on changes should include:','["Only a joke", "Only the date", "What changed, why, and the impact on cost and time", "Nothing"]'::jsonb,2,'Updates keep stakeholders informed.','original'),
('127.94.d.9.G',4,'Presenting the effect of an unexpected delay to the owner helps to:','["Lower quality", "Hide the problem", "Avoid questions", "Maintain trust through transparency"]'::jsonb,3,'Transparency builds confidence.','original'),
('127.94.d.10.A',3,'A project update for stakeholders should be:','["Accurate and timely", "Late", "Vague", "Biased"]'::jsonb,0,'Updates inform decisions.','original'),
('127.94.d.10.A',4,'Stakeholders in a building project may include:','["No one", "Owners, lenders, inspectors, and subcontractors", "Only the crew", "Strangers only"]'::jsonb,1,'Many parties have an interest.','original'),
('127.94.d.10.B',3,'A status report shows:','["Only names", "Only prices", "Progress, issues, and next steps", "Only jokes"]'::jsonb,2,'It summarizes where the project stands.','original'),
('127.94.d.10.B',4,'In a verbal status report, a manager should:','["Skip details", "Talk without structure", "Hide problems", "Be concise and highlight key issues"]'::jsonb,3,'Clear structure helps listeners.','original'),
('127.94.d.11.A',3,'A foreman keeps contact information for the crew in a:','["Contact list or app", "Loose papers", "Memory only", "Nowhere"]'::jsonb,0,'Organized contacts support communication.','original'),
('127.94.d.11.A',4,'Keeping a supplier''s phone number saved in an app helps to:','["Avoid calls", "Reach them quickly when ordering", "Lose it", "Delay orders"]'::jsonb,1,'Accessible info saves time.','original'),
('127.94.d.11.B',3,'A scheduling app can help a foreman to:','["Lose appointments", "Skip meetings", "Plan daily and weekly crew tasks", "Erase plans"]'::jsonb,2,'Calendars organize work.','original'),
('127.94.d.11.B',4,'Setting reminders for inspections helps to:','["Skip safety", "Cause stress", "Delay work", "Avoid missing key dates"]'::jsonb,3,'Reminders improve reliability.','original'),
('127.94.d.11.C',3,'A quick memo on the site should include:','["Date, topic, and action needed", "Only a name", "Only a joke", "Only the weather"]'::jsonb,0,'Memos capture key items.','original'),
('127.94.d.11.C',4,'Notes from a meeting with the owner are useful because they:','["Replace contracts", "Record decisions and responsibilities", "Hide decisions", "Add confusion"]'::jsonb,1,'Notes confirm agreements.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.A',3,'Logging in to a company system requires a:','["Stud finder", "Hammer", "Username and password", "Level"]'::jsonb,2,'Credentials protect access.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.A',4,'A strong password for a jobsite system should be:','["The company name", "''1234''", "Your name", "Long and not easily guessed"]'::jsonb,3,'Strong passwords protect data.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.B',3,'Checking messages from the office each morning helps a crew to:','["Receive updates and changes", "Miss deliveries", "Miss inspections", "Ignore changes"]'::jsonb,0,'Reading messages keeps teams current.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.B',4,'An email from the inspector about a failed inspection should be:','["Deleted unread", "Opened and acted on promptly", "Forwarded to no one", "Ignored"]'::jsonb,1,'Timely response avoids delay.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.C',3,'A professional business email includes:','["All capital letters", "No subject", "A clear subject line and a polite greeting", "Slang only"]'::jsonb,2,'Business standards promote clarity.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.C',4,'A good subject line for an email about concrete delivery is:','["''Hey''", "''Urgent!!!''", "''Stuff''", "''Concrete delivery Friday 8 a.m.''"]'::jsonb,3,'Specific subjects help recipients.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.D',3,'Appropriate email etiquette includes:','["Respectful tone and proofreading", "Rude jokes", "Yelling in caps", "Ignoring grammar"]'::jsonb,0,'Courtesy matters.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.D',4,'Before pressing ''send'' on a message to a client, check for:','["Extra emojis", "Errors and the right recipient", "Nothing", "Slang"]'::jsonb,1,'Review prevents mistakes.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.E',3,'After composing a message, the next step is to:','["Hide it", "Print only", "Send it to the correct recipients", "Delete it"]'::jsonb,2,'Sending delivers the message.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.E',4,'Using ''reply all'' should be reserved for:','["Every message", "Jokes", "Private comments", "Messages that everyone on the thread needs"]'::jsonb,3,'Avoid clutter.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.F',3,'Cloud storage lets a crew:','["Share plans and documents from any device", "Print only", "Lose files", "Hide files"]'::jsonb,0,'Shared files improve coordination.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.F',4,'Sharing a drawing set through a secure link helps to:','["Confuse trades", "Give the team current versions", "Spread outdated copies", "Hide changes"]'::jsonb,1,'Controlled sharing prevents errors.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.G',3,'To open a PDF sent with a message, a worker uses:','["A tape measure", "A crowbar", "The attachment link in the message", "A hammer"]'::jsonb,2,'Attachments hold files.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.G',4,'Before opening an unexpected attachment, check that:','["It is large", "It has a pretty icon", "It is red", "The sender is trusted"]'::jsonb,3,'Unknown files can carry malware.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.H',3,'To send a permit with an email, attach the:','["File from your device", "Paper only", "Nothing", "Hammer"]'::jsonb,0,'Attachments carry documents.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.H',4,'When attaching large plan sets, a better method may be to:','["Send ten copies", "Share a link to cloud storage", "Retype the plans", "Delay indefinitely"]'::jsonb,1,'Links avoid size limits.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.I',3,'Saving messages and attachments helps a contractor to:','["Delay response", "Lose track", "Keep records of decisions", "Avoid proof"]'::jsonb,2,'Records protect the business.','original'),
('127.94.d.12.I',4,'Storing change-order emails in a project folder helps because they:','["Add confusion", "Delete decisions", "Replace contracts", "Document approved changes"]'::jsonb,3,'Organized records show approvals.','original'),
